# Human-maintained source of truth for document-processor's Python
# dependencies. requirements-lock.txt is GENERATED from this file (pip-compile
# --generate-hashes) inside a real Python 3.11 Linux container -- never
# hand-edited. Regenerate whenever this file changes.
#
# torch/torchvision are pinned to the OFFICIAL PyTorch CPU-only wheels via
# direct URL + hash reference, NOT via a global --extra-index-url. This is
# deliberate: adding --extra-index-url to a requirements file exposes EVERY
# other package in this file to dependency-confusion risk (a malicious
# package with the same name could be served from the second index).
# Pinning torch/torchvision to an exact URL + hash instead means only these
# two specific artifacts are sourced from PyTorch's host; every other
# package below resolves exclusively from the default PyPI index.
#
# The default (unpinned-source) `torch` on PyPI resolves to a CUDA-enabled
# Linux wheel that pulls in the full nvidia-*/cuda-toolkit/triton chain
# (~2.5GB+) even though this service is CPU-only (GPU_ENABLED=false,
# no GPU provisioned anywhere) -- confirmed by a real build attempt during
# Step 6B. The CPU-only wheel below has no such dependency at all.
#
# Hashes below were independently verified: downloaded directly from
# download.pytorch.org and re-hashed locally with sha256sum, matching the
# index-published digest exactly (Step 6B CPU-only investigation).
torch @ https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu/torch-2.13.0%2Bcpu-cp311-cp311-manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl \
    --hash=sha256:6746dbcbeb526eb61330b76b41ff1b4eb848951103a892eeb080dfa2b264667b
torchvision @ https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu/torchvision-0.28.0%2Bcpu-cp311-cp311-manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl \
    --hash=sha256:1dad604dfc0177ecebe0891bd9701fe2c62ec3f7819a247be541b3fb6effee99

